# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Shopify Store Configuration
# Copy this file to ".env" and fill in your real credentials.
# The VITE_ prefix exposes these variables to the renderer process.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Full store URL, e.g. https://your-shop.myshopify.com
VITE_SHOPIFY_STORE_URL=

# Admin API access token (starts with shpat_); never commit the real value
VITE_SHOPIFY_ADMIN_API_TOKEN=

# Shopify location id used to scope inventory quantities (gid://shopify/Location/...).
# Auto-detected and cached on first run if left blank.
VITE_SHOPIFY_LOCATION_ID=

# Set to "true" to skip the live Shopify product fetch entirely and seed the
# local catalog with 10 hardcoded demo products instead — the app looks
# fully populated and is scannable for a trial/demo even with no internet
# or Shopify credentials at all. See docs/phase-11.md Task 3.
VITE_DEMO_MODE=false

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Receipt Printer (Phase 5)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Set to "true" to skip hardware and log receipts to the console instead —
# lets a demo proceed without a physical printer.
VITE_MOCK_PRINTER=true

# ESC/POS printer address, e.g. tcp://192.168.0.50:9100
VITE_PRINTER_INTERFACE=tcp://192.168.0.100:9100

# Printed on the receipt header/cashier line.
VITE_STORE_NAME=RUBIS
VITE_CASHIER_NAME=Staff

# Fractional tax rate applied to the subtotal (0.08 = 8%). Defaults to 0.
VITE_TAX_RATE=0

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Kenyan Integrations — M-Pesa / eTIMS (Phase 9)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Each integration has its own mock/real switch. Both default to REAL
# when unset — set to the literal string "true" to select a mock, and
# only a development run will honour it. VITE_USE_MOCK_MPESA selects between
# MockMpesaProvider and DarajaMpesaProvider (Safaricom's Daraja API).
# VITE_USE_MOCK_ETIMS selects between MockFiscalizationProvider and
# RealFiscalizationProvider (the local ZFPLabServer fiscal device
# integration).
#
# As of Phase 42, these two flags are database-backed
# (`app_configurations`, editable via the Admin screen's System tab —
# "Startup Configuration") and only fall back to the env vars below on
# an install with no `.env` and no prior Admin-screen edit (a one-time
# migration seeds the DB from whatever is set here on first launch —
# see `configMigration.ts`). Prefer the Admin screen once the app is
# running; these env vars mainly matter for first-run/unattended
# deploys.
# MUST be exactly "false" (lowercase, no quotes, no leading/trailing spaces)
# to use the real integration — anything else, including "False" or " false",
# is treated as mock. NOTE: once the Admin screen's "Startup Configuration"
# panel has been saved, its DB-stored value takes priority over these env
# vars on every subsequent launch — flip the Admin toggle (or clear the
# `mock_mpesa_enabled`/`mock_etims_enabled` rows in `app_configurations`) if
# changing this file alone has no effect.
#
# POC guidance for eTIMS:
#   - VITE_USE_MOCK_ETIMS=false (below) is the POC default: the real
#     ZFPLabServer integration runs, and any device failure (server
#     unreachable, Code 30 socket failure, Code 31 TCP-password
#     rejection, timeout) still completes the sale and queues the
#     invoice in `sync_queue` for the background fiscal engine to
#     retry. Queued invoices heal themselves once the device is
#     reachable again — no cashier action needed.
#   - Defaults to REAL when absent or blank. Only the literal string
#     'true' selects the mock, and only in a development run: a packaged
#     build never contains the mock fiscalization provider at all, so the
#     flag has no effect there (see `fiscal-provider-factory.ts` and
#     `scripts/verify-no-mock-provider.cjs`).
#
# M-Pesa now works exactly the same way (phase-102). It used to default
# to the MOCK, which approves almost any transaction code — so a till
# installed with no `.env` completed M-Pesa sales for payments that never
# happened. It defaults to REAL, `resolveMpesaProvider` refuses the mock
# in a packaged build, and the same build script fails if the mock is in
# the bundle at all.
#   - To exercise the real wire without a device, leave this at 'false'
#     and run `npm run mock:zfplab` — the real provider talks real HTTP
#     to a local server serving the captured wire fixtures. That is the
#     supported way to demo fiscalization, not the mock provider.
VITE_USE_MOCK_MPESA=false # Defaults to real when absent. 'true' selects the mock in dev builds only.
VITE_USE_MOCK_ETIMS=false # Defaults to real when absent. 'true' selects the mock in dev builds only.

# Daraja credentials, used only when VITE_USE_MOCK_MPESA=false. Prefer
# setting these via the Admin screen's Integrations tab. Non-secret
# fields (consumer key, shortcode, environment, callback URL) are
# stored in the `integrations` table; CONSUMER SECRET and PASSKEY are
# encrypted into the OS credential vault (the same mechanism used for
# the Shopify Admin API token) rather than this table — the env vars
# below are a fallback read only when no vault/DB value is set yet.
# Values below are Safaricom's published Sandbox test credentials.
MPESA_CONSUMER_KEY=
MPESA_CONSUMER_SECRET=
MPESA_SHORTCODE=174379
MPESA_PASSKEY=bfb279f9aa9bdbcf158e97dd71a467cd2e0c893059b10f78e6b72ada1ed2c919
MPESA_ENVIRONMENT=sandbox
MPESA_CALLBACK_URL=https://example.com/callback